::GEO_U06_L04_GP01::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U06_L04_GP01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.15<br><br>Question:<br>A rectangular prism has dimensions 2, 3, and 4. What expression gives its surface area? {
=A. 2(2&middot;3)+2(2&middot;4)+2(3&middot;4)#A rectangular prism has three pairs of congruent rectangular faces.
~B. 2&middot;3&middot;4#That multiplies dimensions for volume, not surface area.
~C. 2+3+4#Adding dimensions does not find surface area.
~D. 4(2+3+4)#This does not account for the areas of all faces.
}

::GEO_U06_L04_GP02::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U06_L04_GP02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.15<br><br>Question:<br>What is the surface area of a cube with side length 5 cm? {
~A. 25 cm&sup2;#This is the area of one face only.
=B. 150 cm&sup2;#A cube has 6 faces, each with area 25 cm&sup2;, so 6(25)=150.
~C. 125 cm&sup3;#That is volume, not surface area.
~D. 30 cm#This is related to edge lengths, not surface area.
}

::GEO_U06_L04_GP03::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U06_L04_GP03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.15<br><br>Question:<br>Which formula gives the total surface area of a cylinder? {
~A. &pi;r&sup2;h#This is cylinder volume.
~B. 2&pi;rh#This is lateral area only, missing the two bases.
=C. 2&pi;r&sup2; + 2&pi;rh#Total surface area includes two circular bases and the curved side.
~D. &pi;rl#This is related to cone lateral area, not cylinder total surface area.
}

::GEO_U06_L04_GP04::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U06_L04_GP04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.15<br><br>Question:<br>A cone surface area problem gives radius and slant height. Which quantity uses slant height? {
~A. Volume#Cone volume uses vertical height, not slant height.
~B. Base area#Base area uses radius only.
~C. Sphere area#A sphere has no slant height.
=D. Lateral area#Cone lateral area uses &pi;rl, where l is slant height.
}

::GEO_U06_L04_GP05::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U06_L04_GP05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.15<br><br>Question:<br>Why must surface area answers use square units? {
=A. Surface area measures the area covering a solid#Surface area is a two-dimensional measurement on the outside of a solid.
~B. Surface area measures capacity#Capacity or volume uses cubic units.
~C. Surface area measures angle opening#Angles use degrees or radians.
~D. Surface area measures only height#Height is linear, but surface area covers faces or curved surfaces.
}
